[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise: they were
merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and a subject
line says that a date is wrong, not why. Read by tenant, form and body, the merged reports are
three problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 fixes the parser only. The other two keep coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants all write the day
  first, so day and month swap: 7 April comes out as 4 July. This is what #4471 describes.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field but reads the date
  day first. People type what the hint says and the date swaps. Only form reports from booking-v3
  tenants. The parser fix does not touch the form.
- **`shift`**: the booking moves by one day, no swap; the same meeting shows Tuesday in Lisbon
  and Monday in Toronto. A timezone or day-boundary bug. The desk already noted these
  (`desk-notes.json`, `oneDayMove`) and filed them under `parser` by tenant.

## How it was counted

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so some reports come twice.
- Cause by tenant locale, booking form and channel (`causes.ts`), not by intake tag. Intake guesses
  from the browser; the table shows how often it guessed a different cause.
- The `shift` reports are the desk's own list, checked against every report body: the others
  quote a day/month swap or no comparable dates.

## For the desk

- Before merging into a ticket, check that the report has the same cause, not the same subject.
  The [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) already shows the difference.
- Reports from booking-v3 forms go to the `hint` ticket, whatever intake tagged them.

